From 8ec908285f64a701511439289178c21daa3b1dfb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: terminills <tdeters@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 27 Jul 2026 18:51:09 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 356/638] [AROS] Wake pumps for delayed work

AI_PHASE: electron-event-loop-coexistence
AI_STATUS: renderer-delayed-work-wake
ROOT_CAUSE: MessagePumpAROS::ScheduleDelayedWork was empty, so Blink timers posted after the renderer entered its wait never woke the pump to recompute and arm timer.device.
FIX_REASON: Reuse ScheduleWork's native Exec signal; Run then recalculates the earliest deadline and uses the existing timer.device wait.
SCOPE: base/message_loop/message_pump_aros.cc
VALIDATION: cef:libcef_static rebuild passes at -j32 in evidence 210; hosted Electron renderer-timer replay follows.
RISK: This may add harmless extra wakeups when a later delayed deadline is posted; Chromium's work deduplicator controls notification frequency.
AI_DECISION_CHAIN: CEF cross-thread posts and Blink timers both stalled -> inspect common AROS pump -> delayed scheduling omitted wake.
Job:
---
 base/message_loop/message_pump_aros.cc | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/base/message_loop/message_pump_aros.cc b/base/message_loop/message_pump_aros.cc
index 2d3b9142c4..56816439d8 100644
--- a/base/message_loop/message_pump_aros.cc
+++ b/base/message_loop/message_pump_aros.cc
@@ -200,7 +200,13 @@ void MessagePumpAROS::ScheduleWork() {
 }
 
 void MessagePumpAROS::ScheduleDelayedWork(
-    const Delegate::NextWorkInfo& next_work_info) {}
+    const Delegate::NextWorkInfo& next_work_info) {
+  // A delayed task may be posted while the pump is blocked indefinitely or
+  // waiting for a later timer deadline. Wake it so Run() can recompute the
+  // earliest deadline and arm timer.device accordingly.
+  (void)next_work_info;
+  ScheduleWork();
+}
 
 void MessagePumpAROS::WaitForIdleEvents(TimeDelta timeout,
                                         bool wait_indefinitely) {
